WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.420
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.400
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.650
Hey, isn't that the moon?

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:11.720
You're right.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.490
It's a midday moon. {no shit, it's there half the month}

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.690
The moon is beautiful at night...

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:18.690
But it's just as beautiful at day.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.380
Seeing it reminds me of Mizuki-san. {not chan?}

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.130
I can't get the Fresh Girls Cup out of my mind either.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:36.640
As I watched her dance, all thoughts of winning or losing just flew away.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.320
I still have a long way to go.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.590
Me too.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:40.960
Same here...

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.140
What're you all spacing out for?

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.030
Suzukawa-san.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.150
Were we really spacing out?

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.030
All the way. To outer space.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.570
We were thinking about Mizuki-san's performance...

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.780
She's unbelievably amazing.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.620
Yeah.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.530
Right.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.300
Well, not like I don't understand. {don't think there's a band-type Mizuki he's talking about}

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.460
But there are girls who look up to you just as much.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.080
They looked at us.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.110
They're all so cute.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.460
I know!

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.470
Don't forget that you're upperclassmen now.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.770
It still doesn't really feel like we're upperclassmen.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:03.700
I know what you mean. Hard to believe we've got juniors now.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.700
We're always caught up in chasing after our senpai.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.310
Wasn't that just Hoshimiya Ichigo?

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:11.880
It was!

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:14.590
Plus Shibuki Ran and Kiriya Aoi!

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:15.980
She used my full name... {uh... I guess it's fine.}

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.650
But thinking back, we did the same thing after we transferred in.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.770
Yeah. It kind of makes me feel like I'm a real idol now.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.970
You <i>are</i> a real idol now.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.220
It still feels like a dream.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.150
Same here.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:32.980
We've got to get our acts together and set a good example now.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.240
<i>Oh no, she has a leaf stuck in her hair...</i>

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.040
What's wrong?

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.370
Nothing... let's go.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:51.970
<i>Oh no, oh no!</i>

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:55.980
<i>The super-cool Aoi-senpai has a leaf stuck in her hair!</i>

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.380
<i>I have no choice but to tell her!</i>

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.890
<i>What am I sneaking around for? Be brave, Akane!</i>

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.860
<i>Why did I hide again?!</i>

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:15.280
<i>I don't want to embarrass her by pointing it out in public...</i>

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.300
<i>I know!</i>

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:20.330
<i>I'll wait for an opportunity and take it out when she isn't looking.</i>

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.380
Oh god, I'm so sorry!

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.790
I promise I'm not some crazy stalker or anything! {I'm not trying to be suspicious}

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:34.920
Don't worry, I know that. So what's wrong?

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.420
Um, well... A-A leaf...

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.640
A leaf?

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.570
You mean this?

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.260
Yes...

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.050
I didn't realize, thanks.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.310
I-I'll be leaving now!

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:52.620
Wait up.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.690
Yes?

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.810
Could you tell me your name?

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.670
I-It's Mimori Akane. Goodbye!

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.950
So her name's Akane-chan. She's pretty cute.

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:04.960
Yeah.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.820
She was following you around to tell you about this.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.110
Probably. But man, I need to get it together.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:15.440
I can't become a senpai who makes her juniors worry.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.710
And for that very same Honey-senpai,

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.090
I have an announcement with good timing. {sorry}

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.800
What do you mean, announcement?

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.830
I'll tell you when we go to the Headmistress's office.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.050
We're going to be teachers?!

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:34.800
That's right. You are all upperclassmen now,

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:38.310
so I believe it would be a good experience to interact with your juniors more.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.580
I understand.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.520
I can't possibly teach a class...

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.440
What kind of material should we prepare for them?

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.650
I leave that up to you.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.140
It's not as if I'm telling you to teach them history or math.

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.450
I want you to teach the first-years about being an idol.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.730
About being an idol?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.710
I'm looking forward to seeing what kind of lesson they'll give.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:09.020
Although they couldn't match Mizuki in the 
Fresh Girls Cup, the three of them were inspiring.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:12.680
Yes. I believe that they matured even more than we realized.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.820
And Kiriya, who's already known for her passionate studying,

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:20.150
is increasing her knowledge base even further through her own experiences.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:24.600
And <i>because</i> it'll be Kiriya, the underclassmen will learn something valuable.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.000
Is that right?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:31.190
And as for Hoshimiya and Shibuki, don't you get excited just thinking about what kind of lessons they'll give?

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.120
Now that's just you having fun. {not really at their expense}

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.990
What do I do? I'm not cut out to be a teacher...

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:43.540
I have no idea what I should teach the first-years.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.050
I just want to teach them something useful.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.350
Yeah. And looking back now,

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:53.760
we've learned so much from our senpai like Mizuki-san and Ema-san.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:54.560
True.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.880
But that was outside the classroom.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.560
I can't possibly wear a suit and high heels and be a teacher...

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:03.560
Good morning, first-years.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.090
I'll be your teacher starting today.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.570
No way! That's impossible!

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.720
Well...

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:13.570
Nobody said you have to wear high heels.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.330
So what am I supposed to do?

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.550
I mean...

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.080
No idea.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.240
I wonder what they're talking about?

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.310
I bet it's about their next gig.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:24.840
They look so serious!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.590
This is bad. I can't think of anything no matter how hard I try.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:34.600
Same here.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.600
What do you think they want to learn about?

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.230
Back then, what sort of things were we curious about?

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:42.730
Everything!

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.610
That doesn't get us anywhere.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:47.440
How about we ask a first-year what they want?

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.340
Good idea! {were you talking to yourself again?}

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.060
Sakura-chan!

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:52.950
Yes?

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.420
Is there anything you'd like to ask us?

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:57.840
Anything is fine.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:02.460
If there's anything you want to ask us 
upperclassmen, then please go ahead.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.330
I don't believe I have anything like that.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.670
I learn plenty just from following your example.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.010
I'm constantly improving because of you. {I didn't like the re-use of "learn" but couldn't find a way to make it better}

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:18.750
No go, Sakura-chan's already got it together.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:21.840
We could learn a few things from <i>her</i> if we wanted.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:26.490
Isn't there anyone else we know who embodies a "first-year" more? {I don't know, how about your little sisters? Marimite reference}

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.570
Um, so...

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.780
Do you have some business with me?

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.720
Sorry about this.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:43.500
The three of us are going to be giving a lesson on being an idol to the first-years.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:50.340
We want to know what you and your friends would like to learn from us.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:52.910
Akane-chan?

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:54.010
Are you okay?

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.820
Of course, I'm just so happy!

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.140
I'm so grateful!

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.000
Hey...

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.510
What's up?

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.400
Why are you crying?

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.150
F-Forgive me... But I'm truly moved.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:10.170
I'm so happy to have a chance to be taught by you.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:13.900
I don't know anything about the world of idols yet.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:18.220
When I saw your earnest faces at the cafeteria earlier,

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.910
I thought you were so amazing.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.870
Anything's fine.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.550
The things you've seen, or the things you've felt,

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:28.090
no matter what you decide to teach us,

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:30.800
I'll be so happy that I'll cry.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.720
Akane-chan really is cute.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:35.700
Yeah.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:40.980
But what should we do? Even if anything's fine, that doesn't help us pick a topic.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.310
We won't get an answer like this.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.710
Oh man...

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.730
We've got no choice but to try.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.630
I've collected a lot of knowledge about idols through the years,

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:51.860
but now that I have experience doing things myself

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.070
I've realized that there are a lot of differences between theory and practice.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:58.070
They might enjoy it if I teach them things like that.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:02.080
That sounds good. I'll try talking about my own experiences too.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.330
I think that's a good idea too.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.860
Alright, let's do this.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:09.000
I'll be happy if even one of them is able to learn from me.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:09.750
Yeah.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.090
Right.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.470
Let's see...

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:27.980
I've got makeup, mouth wash, and my lucky charm.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.010
What're you doing?

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.980
I'm checking the things that I take to auditions.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.990
Hey, that's not a charm, isn't it just your rice scoop?

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.840
It's my own personal charm.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:44.740
I calm down when I hold it, and it gives me the courage to do my best.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.450
Then it really is important.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:49.020
I get so nervous at auditions I could die,

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:53.890
and I'd regret it if I couldn't put on my best performance, so I always take it with me.

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:55.570
Only you, Ichigo.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:59.970
Though I bet there are times when you panic and forget it too.

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.640
What are you going to teach, Ran?

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.770
I think I'm just going to tell them to ask whatever questions they want.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.020
So cool!

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.460
You're so famous, I think it'll work.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:15.270
I'm sure the first-years have a lot to ask you.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.670
I'm not sure if it'll actually help them though.

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:21.330
That's not true at all! And besides, you're a lot nicer than you look.

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:23.260
I've learned a lot from you.

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:25.150
What do you mean, "nicer than I look"?

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:28.260
Well I mean, you were a bit hard to approach when I first met you.

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:31.540
Really? I seem to remember you clinging on to me from the start.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.540
Really? Did I?

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:37.550
We had only heard of you as the Beautiful Blade, {haven't heard that in a while}

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:40.010
so it really was hard to talk to you.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.830
It was surprising how well you take care of others.

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:45.510
Enough of that. So Aoi, what about you?

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:51.220
I... I'll talk about the things I've seen while doing TV and movie work

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:53.680
that might not be obvious at first glance.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:59.210
I've even got this diary full of good material.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.930
You were keeping a diary?

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:04.920
I call it a diary, but it's really a lifelog in notebook form.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:07.260
Life... what?

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:11.490
A notebook full of what I experience and feel every day.

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:12.920
I wanna see!

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.640
No! It's embarrassing.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:18.340
Why? You're going to be telling the first-years anyway.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:22.050
Does it even matter? You've been with Aoi this entire time.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.390
Oh yeah, you're right.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:27.310
I want to teach the first-years whatever I can.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:28.060
Yeah!

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:29.560
Right!

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.560
And then the day of our lesson came.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.560
What do I do?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.020
I'm more nervous than I am at auditions. {wakaru, wakaru}

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:38.070
What's with that?

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:41.600
If I mess up and say something stupid

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:43.820
they'll all laugh at me...

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:48.020
You'll be fine. You're the type who can pull it all together under pressure.

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:50.510
Go out there with the intent to make them laugh.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:52.330
Alright, I'll do it.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:57.240
I can't wait for their lesson to start!

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:00.250
I've never heard Shibuki Ran's voice in person.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.880
Thank god I entered Starlight Academy!

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.650
I'm more interested in Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:08.350
She was amazing in the Fresh Girls Cup!

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:13.350
<i>I've gotta record every last word of what they say!</i>

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:15.600
Okay, I'm off.

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:16.900
Good luck.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.790
Be careful not to fall.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.860
She isn't you, you know.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:33.370
Shibuki-sensei, we'll be in your care!

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:38.290
Y-You don't need to address me like I'm a teacher. {where did your amagami training go}

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:42.050
Now, if there's anything you'd like me to talk about,

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.880
feel free to ask anything.

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:46.030
You're so cool!

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.630
Shibuki-senpai!

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.890
Wait, um, questions...

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:02.610
How was it?

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:03.650
Were you nervous?

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:07.220
Well, er... good luck.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:08.410
They're amazing.

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:10.800
What do you mean?

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.610
You're up, Ichigo. Don't keep them waiting.

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:14.660
Okay...

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:21.170
Good afternoon, everyone. {considering this is sort of a point}

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:22.510
What's that?

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:23.280
A rice scoop?

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:24.170
Cute!

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:28.430
<i>Everyone's looking at me... I need to be careful not to fall over.</i>

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.580
So cute!

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:33.880
Don't give up!

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:35.810
Ichigo-chan, fight! {that's very miku-ish hair}

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:37.850
Are you alright?

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.810
Thanks, everyone!

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.310
I'm back!

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.590
Well?

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:45.070
They were amazing, right?

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:48.700
Yeah! I was moved by how much they cheered me on.

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:50.790
Cheered?

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:51.860
Yeah!

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:52.950
What about the lesson?

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.330
Well, I...

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:59.040
You sang a song and then came back?!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.080
Yeah... they asked me so nicely, so...

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:05.460
Everyday's a special day!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:09.950
I don't know whether to be amazed or say I expected it.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:11.220
Aoi, it's on you now.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.730
Alright, leave it to me.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:24.700
Aoi-chan's wearing glasses!

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:25.860
Cute...

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.570
Aoi-sensei...

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.160
Good morning.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.160
Good morning.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:41.810
I'm sure you're all aware, but the standard greeting in the entertainment industry

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:45.170
is "good morning", no matter what time of day it is.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:48.630
For me, no matter what time my job may start,

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:52.080
I've made it an important aspect of myself to brighten up the day

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.740
with a fresh "good morning".

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:58.030
Don't you agree that it makes everyone else feel better that way?

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:02.670
When I have work at a TV station, even if I don't know the person

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:05.650
I say "good work" when I pass by.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:09.820
I was a bit embarrassed to talk to people like that at the beginning,

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.700
but I want you to be brave and try the same.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:16.420
Each and every greeting makes both you and those around you smile.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:19.410
Rookies should show their freshness

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:22.210
with a bright and happy greeting every day.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:26.250
I never knew there was a reason behind the way they greet people in the industry.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.770
The most important thing about choosing your appearance at auditions

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.760
is to search for the best way to bring out your true self.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:39.220
Every single audition is a new chance to learn more about yourself.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:42.220
It's the accumulation of daily study.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:45.850
Kiriya's lesson is quite educational.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:48.480
What are we supposed to say if we have to learn from her? {1) not a good line 2) teachers are supposed to learn} {not in japan}

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:52.860
But Kiriya has really met my expectations of being a teacher.

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:56.910
How was it?

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.120
Seems like everyone listened quietly to you.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:02.830
Yeah. And I may not be Ichigo, but I was moved.

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:04.960
Why's that?

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:07.200
They told me after I finished,

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:10.710
"I want to become an idol just like you."

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:13.960
Wow, no wonder you're happy.

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:18.720
Yeah. We may have gotten a bit gloomy after seeing Mizuki-san's performance,

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.520
but it's no time for us to be feeling down!

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:21.230
Yeah!

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:22.200
Right!

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.480
Listen, honeys.

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:28.110
Sensei!

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:33.490
We got you honeys a special present as a reward for your hard work.

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:35.110
Take these.

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:38.490
Rare cards from the Spring Collection!

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:41.490
They're calming yet glamorous.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:44.500
Wow, there are so many frills and ribbons!

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.000
They're so gorgeous!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.980
It's a reward for giving such a good lesson.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:54.380
Now go out there and show the first-years the best performance you can give.

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:55.830
Yes!

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.160
That felt great!

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:51.930
Yeah.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:52.850
Right.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:55.820
It really is the best when we're all together.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:56.970
I agree.

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:57.710
Same here.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:01.690
That was a great performance!

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:07.070
Thanks for listening so intently to our lessons today.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.860
N-Not at all! {does this work?}

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:11.230
Thank you for teaching us so much.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.790
Akane-chan?

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:17.060
You okay?

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:18.720
Do you feel sick?

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:20.510
That's not it...

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:22.380
Then why are you crying?

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:27.390
I... every single day I was so, so worried...

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:31.610
I thought I might not be cut out to become an idol.

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:37.280
But after listening to your lessons and watching your live performance,

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:41.650
I thought from the bottom of my heart that I want to have fun like that too.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:43.870
So I'll start giving everything I have!

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:46.400
I'll aim to become an idol just like you!

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:49.120
Great! Let's both do our best.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.660
Aoi-sensei...

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.140
Sensei?

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:58.490
Yes, you'll always be my Aoi-sensei. Thank you very much!

00:22:06.610 --> 00:22:08.290
Akane-chan's pretty cute, huh?

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.070
Right, Aoi-sensei?

00:22:10.070 --> 00:22:13.430
Stop calling me that, I'm just their senpai.

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:18.710
I'm sure a lot more wonderful first-years like Akane-chan are going to come to us now.

00:22:18.710 --> 00:22:20.500
We have to do our best.

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:21.470
Right!

00:22:21.470 --> 00:22:22.440
Yeah!

00:23:55.710 --> 00:23:57.870
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:01.470
No matter what time it is, you say "good morning" in the entertainment industry.

00:24:01.470 --> 00:24:03.070
It literally means "Early, isn't it?"

00:24:03.070 --> 00:24:05.610
So it isn't strange no matter what time it is.

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:07.460
It's a really versatile greeting!

00:24:08.070 --> 00:24:10.010
Treasure your greetings!

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:12.160
"Call and lettuce ponzu"?

00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:13.300
No, no!

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:14.680
Call and response!

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:16.900
If you get it, say "Woo!"

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:17.810
Woo!

00:24:18.130 --> 00:24:19.680
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:21.820
A sincere call and response.

00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:24.110
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
